  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Bale Eye" id="4f5f-5c0a-804b-094c" hidden="false" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Can be used once at the start of each close combat phase. It automatically hits any one model engaged with Yarrick in close combat</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Baneblade Tank Damage Table" id="bf6c-a4b6-9587-db1c" hidden="false" page="datafax">
      <description>1: Tracks
2-4: Hull
5: Sponsons*
6: Volcano Cannon
*Hit&apos;s closest to the shooter
See datafax for damage table results</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Barrage" id="80be-65f8-fa8b-eb31" hidden="false" page="71" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>At start of turn 1 roll a D6. On a 2+, mark down the number as the interference level. If you roll a 1, re-roll until you get a 2+.

From turn 2 and onwards, can call 1 Barrage for each commanding officer whose squad includes a comm-link. Roll a D6 and if you equal or beat your established interference level you may call in the barrage.

See Codex Imperial Guard Pg. 71 for further instructions on dropping Barrage</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bodyguard" id="556f-45d1-0f3d-322b" hidden="false" page="86" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Any shooting hit on the commander can be taken by Deddog if he is within 2&quot;. The player may decide wheather to work out the shot against Deddog or his commander</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Chenkov" id="b772-131b-500b-4349" hidden="false" page="88" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Allowed re-rolls for any Leadership based tests (break, psychology, rally, etc.). 
At the start of the game the Imperial Guard player rolls a D6. That score is the number of re-rolls he is permitted during the game. These can be used any time as long as Chenkov is still alive.

As long as Chenkov is still alive, one reroll is added every time the enemy receives victory points for wiping out or breaking a unit. Note that no bonus is earned for reducing a unit to half strength, only for wiping it out or breaking it.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Crazed" id="cf86-5c39-f34b-c137" hidden="false" page="69" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Ignore psychology tests and do not make Break test unles they lose half their number during the current turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Dead Eye Shots" id="4c12-fb71-25b1-a348" hidden="false" page="69" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Any trooper who misses a shot can re-roll the dice to hit. This does not apply to grenades or heavy weapons that use a blast marker</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Demolisher Cannon" id="2db6-c329-1625-e85f" hidden="false" page="23" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>+3 to roll on any datafax damage tables. Results modified above 6 count as 6
Cannot move and fire, but the tank may fire other weapons as normal when moving.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Earthshaker" id="19be-4f44-60e8-ad0d" hidden="false" page="27" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Fires two shells, pick a target within the 45° fire arc. Roll to hit for each shell, scattering as normal if you miss.
When hitting a target using a datafax (such as vehicles, buildings) roll for armour penetration as normal. If penetrated, roll a D6 on the damage table. If not penetrated, roll a D3 on the damage table.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Freedom Fighters" id="0c84-d718-25ed-1f21" hidden="false" page="69" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>If Freedom Fighter&apos;s are inside a wood, or within a building, then each enemy model that moves within the same terrain suffers a strength 3 hit. Ogryn&apos;s cannot be Freedom Fighters.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Grizzled" id="528d-5a12-7a4c-68e0" hidden="false" page="69" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Roll 3 dice instead of 2 for Leadership test and pick the best 2.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Guerrillas" id="404d-9371-e4d3-bcfd" hidden="false" page="69" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>May run and hide in the same turn or, alternatively, run and shoot with a -1 to hit penalty. Not available to Ogryns</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hardened Fighters" id="29d6-32bf-35ff-2fdf" hidden="false" page="69" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>May re-roll a single Attack dice. Opponents may never parry against a Hardened Fighter&apos;s attack.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Heavy Mortar" id="6789-9aed-b2d9-4fe6" hidden="false" page="24" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>See Imperial Guard Codex pg. 24 for rules on firing the heavy mortar</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hellhound Damage Table" id="3958-84e7-8e69-82ed" hidden="false" page="datadax" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>1-2: Track
3-4: Hull
5-6: Turret
See datafax for damage table results</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hot Headed" id="31e0-4bfd-49a9-077c" hidden="false" page="83" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>When Macharius charges, instead of a +1 modifier add D6. This only applies if he charges</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Immune to Psychology" id="a27d-0ce7-d623-31ab" hidden="false">
      <description>Immune to the Psychology rules given in the Warhammer 40k rulebook. They cannot be affected by Fear, Terror, Etc.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Imperial Basilisk" id="fe4d-2bc7-df5e-2b71" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>1-2: Track - Hit closest to attacker
3-5: Hull
6: Earthshaker
See datafax for damage table results</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Imperial Chimera Damage Table" id="13bb-d4c7-8c1f-0ff2" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>1-2 Track - Hit closest to shooter
3-5: Hull
6: Turret
See datafax for damage table results</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Imperial Griffon Damage Table" id="da09-f549-a92b-6728" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>1-2: Track - Hit closest to attacker
3-5: Hull
6: Heavy Mortar/ Crew - Roll a further D6, 1-3 Mortar is hit, 4-6 Crew is hit
See datafax for damage table results</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Imperial Guard Land Speeder Damage Table" id="ce15-e4dc-144f-8513" hidden="false" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>1-2: Crew*
3-6: Land Speeder
*Hit closest to attacker
See datafax for damage table results</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Imperial Guard Sentinel Damage Table" id="fc84-b17f-5137-c39c" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>1-2: Legs
3: Assault Cannon
4-5: Body
6: Imperial Guardsman
See datafax for damage table results</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Inferno Cannon" id="33d0-b03b-af0c-3b58" hidden="false" page="26" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Place the Heavy Flamer Template as normal, then roll an Artillery Die and move the template that many inches straight ahead. The normal rules for templates apply to models touched or covered by the template at any point in its movement. Models surviving a hit may still catch on fire.
In addition, crew inside vehicles affected by the Inferno Cannon may be affected even if the armour is not
penetrated. For each model on board, roll D6; on a 6, the model takes 1 wound with a –1 save modifier. If a
location catches fire, you must continue to test for the crew until the flames go out.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Inferno Shell" id="81c4-56e2-c519-9ec6" hidden="false" page="25" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>If a model hit by an Inferno shell is not killed, roll a D6. On a 4+ they are lit on fire.
For the model that was lit on fire, on it&apos;s turn check the Fire Test Table:
1-5: Take a further hit from the same weapon profile. If not slain, move it randomly and it cannot do anything else that turn. Vehicles, Dreadnoughts, and Terminators can ignore the flames and move &amp; fire as normal.
6: Fire goes out. The model may not move nad fire during the current turn but may fight normally from its following turn onwards. Vehicles, Dreadnoughts, and Terminators can ignore the flames and move &amp; fire as normal.

See Imperial Guard rulebook pg.25 for further burn rules</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Iron Will" id="42f7-0fcf-ac0a-6875" hidden="false" page="85" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>If Yarrick suffers a hit which reduces his Wounds to 0, roll a D6:
1-4: Restore Yarrick to 1 Wound and continue fighting
5-6: Remove the model as a casualty</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Killer Shot" id="6212-e526-40a2-85c9" hidden="false" page="89" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>As an alternative to firing D3 times, Stumper can go for one carefully placed shot. Shoot as normal, if the shot hits then the enemies armour save is reduced by a further D3.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Leaders" id="17f1-a1dc-e584-8ea0" hidden="false" page="20" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Commissar can move from one squad to another. A squad with a Commissar can always test its Leadership against the Commissar&apos;s value of 10</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Leadership" id="9608-a7aa-cd1c-44df" hidden="false" page="67" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Any Imperial Guard unit within 12&quot; of this model may take Break tests using their Leadership value</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Leman Russ Battle Tank Damage Table" id="8016-e9b0-00af-6a52" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>1: Track
2-3: Hull
4: Heavy Bolter
5-6: Turret
See datafax for damage table results</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Leman Russ Demolisher Damage Table" id="4811-30e5-99ed-a450" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>1: Track
2-3: Hull
4: Side Sponson - Hit side closer to attacker
5-6: Turret
See datafax for damage table results</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Lord Commander" id="ecf1-48e9-acbd-c1c3" hidden="false" page="83" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Automatically pass any leadership test he is required to take on his own behalf. 
Immune to all psychology and cannot be affected by fear, terror, etc the same ways as a Commissar
Cannot be broken and never take a Break test

Any Imperial Guard unit within 12&quot; may use his Leadership when taking a Break Test</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mortar" id="f35a-5c43-277e-ca0e" hidden="false" page="22" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>See Imperial Guard Codex pg. 22 for rules on firing the mortar</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ripper Gun" id="638a-66a8-1c3f-079f" hidden="false" page="28" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>No &quot;to hit&quot; dice is needed at short range, automatically hits.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rough Rider Standard" id="2959-83d2-2aaa-10bb" hidden="false" page="18" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>If unit includes a standard, all Rough Riders in the unit may add +1 to their close combat score</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shaefer&apos;s Last Chancers" id="8f69-e1e7-0623-67ad" hidden="false" page="89" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Shaefer and his penal squad form a single unit and must remain within normal unit coherency at all times. So long as the colonel is alive the entire squad will automatically pass any Leadership based tests (Break tests, psychology, rally, etc). This includes a divided heavy wepaons team which still continues to benefit as long as Colonel Shaefer is alive. 
So long as Shaefer is alive any member of the Penal squad may re-roll any miss when shooting and any fumbles in close combat. The re-rolled score must be accepted, even if it is another miss or another fumble.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Slick Crew" id="308c-2bdd-bb68-0765" hidden="false" page="69" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>If the weapon scores a hit then it is automatically entitled to a further shot that shooting phase (as long as it does not jam, explode, need to charge, etc.) The extra shot can be against the same target, or any new target that could otherwise be fired at. Finish the results of the 1st before doing the 2nd.

For mortars they only get a second shot if their first round is a direct hit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Squads" id="6430-a48e-b9d1-90f3" hidden="false" page="20" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Although they are characters psykers must always fight as part of a Command squad or a Command HQ as described</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Stealthy" id="a6d9-68d0-0323-30a4" hidden="false" page="69" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Stealthy troops ignore all movement penalties for difficult or very difficult terrain. They also receive a +1 combat score in close combat when fighting in such terrain. In addition, their line of sight is increased to 4&quot; through wood. 
May not be used by Rough Riders or Ogryns.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Strategy" id="7eaa-9e5e-0325-4818" hidden="false" page="83" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Roll a D6 to determine Macharius&apos; strategy rating before the game beginns
1-3: Reserves and barrages are worked out as described by the rules.
4-5: No barrage is permitted before the game
6: No barrage is permitted before the game and all reserves must be deployed onto the tabletop immediately.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Street Fighters" id="6cb7-47a3-c920-84ed" hidden="false" page="69" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Street Fighters in soft cover count -2 to hit and when in hard cover they count -3 to hit. May not be used by Rough Riders</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tank Hunters" id="a666-22cb-c942-4ee2" hidden="false" page="69" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>When Tank Hunters use grenades against vehicles they may automatically re-roll any or all of the dice for armour penetration. Tank Hunters also ignore any psychological effects that may be caused by vehicles.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tech Priest Engineer - Repair" id="b688-369b-5af2-8115" hidden="false" page="44" publicationId="d829-388d-3717-5aca">
      <description>May attempt to repair a single damaged hit location on a vehicle, dreadnought, or a destroyed support weapon, if they can reach it during their next movement phase. They can do nothin else that turn they attempt to repair. At the end of the turn roll a D6:

1-2: Hopeless - Nothing happens
3-4: Possible Repair - Damaged not repairs this turn but may continue trying next turn. If attempting again on the next turn it will suceed on a 4+, or else becomes a Hopeless result
5-6: Repairs the damage</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Trick Shot" id="4d33-3457-b331-20cc" hidden="false" page="89" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>At the start of the shooting phase roll a D3 to determine how many shots he can fire that turn. These shots can be directed against any enemy target in sight regardless of which models are the closest. Nominate which models will be shot at before rolling any dice to hit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Very Loyal" id="ee7f-011f-89fb-f6a1" hidden="false" page="86" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>So long as Nork&apos;s commander is alive he must remain within 2&quot; of him at all times when possible</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Yarrick" id="2306-e749-3ae0-bab0" hidden="false" page="85" publicationId="a1e3-886b-e509-d15a">
      <description>Can move freely from squad to squad. Any squad with Commissar Yarrick will automatically pass any Leadership test it is required to take. 

Any unit that can see Commissar Yarrick will automatically pass any Leadership test. However, Yarrick must be closer to the enemy than the unit itself for this rule to apply.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Guardsman Bike Damage Table" id="b685-99e5-2e09-4baf" hidden="false">
      <description>1-2: Crew is hit
3-6: Bike is hit
See datafax for damage table</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rhino Damage Table" id="e188-67a4-8b10-3876" hidden="false" page="Datafax">
      <description>1: Track - Closest track to shooter
2-5: Hull
6: Weapons
See datafax for damage table</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Land Raider Damage Table" id="cda7-9804-44df-7f43" hidden="false" page="Datafax">
      <description>1-2: Track - Hit closest to shooter
3-5: Hull
6: Lascannon - Hit closest to shooter
See datafax for damage table</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Predator Damage Table" id="d2a8-84c5-78a2-b651" hidden="false">
      <description>1: Track - Closest track to shooter
2-3: Hull
4: Sponson - Closest track to shooter
5-6: Turret
See datafax for damage table</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
  <sharedSelectionEntries>
    <selectionEntry name="Tech-Priest Engineer" id="2b87-3654-70db-fd42" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="model">
      <comment>Black Codex</comment>
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink name="Imperial Guard" id="7b60-943a-7d75-5b6d" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="ef00-5e3b-a59a-902f"/>
        <categoryLink name="1Characters" id="d148-6f67-c0bc-5516" hidden="false" primary="true" targetId="7576-d91f-083c-38a7"/>
